A background's last line doesn't show the image past the frame when
upscaled (warecomp STATUS.md rounds 12 and 13).

S2DEX bg1Cyc draws a background in slices, loading one line more than it
draws when bilerp is on. The RDP samples each pixel at its top, so that
extra line only ever gets a zero weight; drawn at a higher resolution, the
lower part of each output line samples further down. Inside the frame the
line below is the frame's own next line, but on the frame's last line it is
the image past the frame: Worms Armageddon's level showed a sliver of the
level below the screen (or the level's top border, where the image wraps)
along the bottom edge of the window. In the frame's last slice, the TMEM
line after the last line it shows now gets a copy of that line.

(Clamping T at that line instead, the first version, lost the last line of
small frames such as the game's name tags in RT64's sampling.)

--- a/src/gbi/rt64_gbi_s2dex.cpp
+++ b/src/gbi/rt64_gbi_s2dex.cpp
@@ -391,8 +391,25 @@
                         imageSliceH = std::min(imageSliceH, imageSliceLines);
                     }
 
+                    const uint32_t sliceImagePtr = imagePtr;
                     bg1CycTMEMLoad(*rdp, scaleBg, imageAddress, imagePtr, imageRemain, imageSrcWsize, imagePtrX0, tmemSrcLines, tmemSliceWmax, imageSliceH, usesBilerp, flagSplit);
 
+                    // The frame's last slice: the TMEM line after the last image line it shows gets a copy of
+                    // that line. The RDP samples each pixel at its top, so the line after only ever gets a zero
+                    // weight, but drawn at a higher resolution the bottom of the frame's last line samples
+                    // further down and showed the image past the frame (the next line of the image, or its top
+                    // where it wraps). With the copy it samples the same line again.
+                    if ((frameRemain <= 0) && (scaleBg.imageSiz != G_IM_SIZ_32b)) {
+                        const int32_t lastLineT = (int32_t(imageT) + (((frameSliceH - 1) * int32_t(scaleH)) >> 5)) >> 5;
+                        const int32_t copyLine = lastLineT + 1;
+                        if ((lastLineT >= 0) && ((copyLine + 1) * int32_t(tmemSliceWmax) <= tmemSize)) {
+                            const int32_t sliceStartLine = int32_t(sliceImagePtr - imageAddress - imagePtrX0) / int32_t(imageSrcWsize);
+                            const int32_t lastImageLine = (((sliceStartLine + lastLineT) % int32_t(tmemSrcLines)) + int32_t(tmemSrcLines)) % int32_t(tmemSrcLines);
+                            const uint32_t lastLinePtr = imageAddress + uint32_t(lastImageLine) * imageSrcWsize + imagePtrX0;
+                            bg1CycTMEMSetAndLoadTile(*rdp, scaleBg, lastLinePtr, imageSrcWsize, 1, tmemSliceWmax, int16_t(copyLine * tmemSliceWmax), tmemSliceWmax);
+                        }
+                    }
+
                     int16_t framePtrY1 = framePtrY0 + frameSliceH;
                     rdp->drawTexRect(frameX0, framePtrY0 << 2, frameX1, framePtrY1 << 2, G_TX_RENDERTILE, imageS, imageT, scaleW, scaleH, false);
                     framePtrY0 = framePtrY1;
